  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe Mazak post starts and stops the spindle with `MOTON S..` and `MOTOFF` in every section:\n\n```\nT2 M6\nG43 H2\nMOTON S600\nM8\nG00 X0 Y0 Z20\nG99\nG84 X0 Y0 Z8 R20 F600\nG80\nG00 X0 Y0 Z45\nM9\nMOTOFF\n```\n\nThese are the only multi-letter words in the program. The post's own header gives its grammar as \"public RS-274/ISO 6983 documentation\". In that grammar a word is an address letter followed by a number (`M3`, `S600`), so `MOTON` and `MOTOFF` are not words of it.\n\n`MOTON` also states no direction. The block after it is a right-hand rigid tap (`G84`), which needs the spindle turning clockwise.\n\n## Reproduction (main 38699549, `camcraft-cli mcp`)\n\n`assets/posts/mazak.cps` is unchanged from there to 3f6ecb4a.\n\nThe part is a Ø36 × 20 disc with a Ø5 blind hole to z 4. On the built-in `VMC 3-axis`:\n\n- **D1:** Drill with `cycle: \"peck\"`, `peck: 2`.\n- **D2:** Drill with `cycle: \"drill\"`, `dwell: 0.5`.\n- **T1:** Drill with `TAP-M6`, `cycle: \"tap\"`, threaded to z 8.\n\n`generate` and `verify` are clean. `post` with `\"post\": \"Mazak\"` writes 49 lines, with `MOTON S7500` / `MOTON S600` and `MOTOFF` around each section as above. The words have been in the post since it shipped (4288300f, M3.3 B), and the goldens under `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/mazak/` lock them.\n\n## Neighbour case\n\nThe same stream through the other Fanuc-family posts (`Fanuc`, `Haas`, `doosan-dnm.cps`, `tormach.cps`) writes `S600 M3` before the tap and `M5` at section end.\n\n## Root cause (unknown)\n\nThe header credits the words to \"the control family's published operator conventions\" (\"spindle-logic M words MOTON/MOTOFF with the speed on the same block\"), but names no document. I found no public Mazak EIA/ISO material that uses them. If a Mazak control does not accept them, every program from this post fails at its first spindle start. That is either an alarm, or feeds with the spindle stopped if the block is skipped.\n\nWhich published Mazak document gives `MOTON` / `MOTOFF` as the spindle start and stop words?\n\n## Suggested labels\n\nOutside contributors can't set labels, so these are suggestions:\n\n- `P1` if the words are not Mazak's (wrong posted G-code in every Mazak program). The question above settles that.\n- `effort:high`: posted G-code.\n- `area:post`\n- `source:agent`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
